From 01c85918eb6b84db54a1a59c57c114498497668a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lorenzo Giannoccaro <giannoccarol@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 11:33:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] libbt-vendor: use the unprefixed wc_transport properties

The msm8994 wcnss_filter blob reads and sets wc_transport.*; with the
vendor. prefix the filter never starts and Bluetooth times out. Also
drop BT_NV_SUPPORT so the address comes from /persist/bdaddr.txt as on
Android 13.

Change-Id: Id1b9b1253402881553266b7abee17364e5f56694
---
 libbt-vendor/Android.bp | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libbt-vendor/Android.bp b/libbt-vendor/Android.bp
index 3ba0159..613daa0 100644
--- a/libbt-vendor/Android.bp
+++ b/libbt-vendor/Android.bp
@@ -12,8 +12,7 @@ cc_library_shared {
     vendor: true,
 
     cflags: [
-        "-DBT_NV_SUPPORT",
-        "-DBT_NV_SUPPORT_DL",
+        "-DUSE_OLD_WCNSS_FILTER",
         "-Wno-enum-conversion",
         "-Wno-incompatible-pointer-types-discards-qualifiers",
         "-Wno-unused-function",
-- 
2.56.0

